---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FAQSection from '../components/FAQSection.astro';
import { faqSchema } from '../data/faqs';

const pageTitle = 'End of Abyss Platforms: PS5, Xbox Series X/S, PC & Nintendo Switch 2';
const pageDescription = 'Complete platform breakdown for End of Abyss. Compare graphics modes, PS5 DualSense haptics, Xbox performance, PC specs, and Nintendo Switch 2 release rumors.';
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} schema={[faqSchema]}>
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 space-y-12">
    
    <!-- Hero / Header -->
    <div class="space-y-4 border-b border-abyss-border pb-8">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-abyss-hazard/15 border border-abyss-hazard/40 text-abyss-hazard text-xs font-mono font-bold tracking-wider uppercase">
        <span>Hardware & Cross-Platform Specs</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white font-mono tracking-tight">
        End of Abyss Platform Guide
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Whether you are playing on high-end PC, experiencing adaptive trigger haptics on PlayStation 5, or tracking the anticipated Nintendo Switch 2 launch, here is the complete platform breakdown for <em>End of Abyss</em>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Platform Cards Grid -->
    <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      
      <!-- PlayStation 5 -->
      <div class="hud-card rounded-2xl p-6 border border-abyss-border space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-mono">
            PlayStation 5
          </span>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-abyss-card border border-abyss-border text-slate-300">Available</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          The PS5 edition of End of Abyss makes extensive use of the DualSense controller. Each weapon has distinctive adaptive trigger resistance (the Arc Shotgun requires a heavy pull with physical kickback), and haptic vibrations convey bio-anomaly footsteps crawling under floor grates.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-abyss-void/80 p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-abyss-border space-y-1 text-xs font-mono text-slate-300">
          <div><strong>Resolution Mode:</strong> Dynamic 4K @ 60 FPS</div>
          <div><strong>Performance Mode:</strong> 1440p @ 120 Hz Target</div>
          <div><strong>Audio:</strong> Tempest 3D Audio binaural positional sound</div>
        </div>
        <a
          href="https://store.playstation.com/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="w-full py-2.5 px-4 rounded-xl bg-white hover:bg-slate-200 text-black font-semibold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-center block transition-colors shadow-md"
        >
          <span>View on PlayStation Store ↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Xbox Series X|S -->
      <div class="hud-card rounded-2xl p-6 border border-abyss-border space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-mono">
            Xbox Series X | S
          </span>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-abyss-card border border-abyss-border text-slate-300">Available</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Full support for Quick Resume across subterranean save terminals. The Xbox Series X runs at native 4K with ray-traced ambient occlusion, while the compact Series S targets smooth 1080p 60 FPS with reconstructed lighting.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-abyss-void/80 p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-abyss-border space-y-1 text-xs font-mono text-slate-300">
          <div><strong>Series X:</strong> Native 4K @ 60 FPS / VRR Supported</div>
          <div><strong>Series S:</strong> Dynamic 1080p @ 60 FPS</div>
          <div><strong>Features:</strong> Quick Resume &amp; Dolby Atmos spatial audio</div>
        </div>
        <a
          href="https://www.xbox.com/games/store/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="w-full py-2.5 px-4 rounded-xl bg-white hover:bg-slate-200 text-black font-semibold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-center block transition-colors shadow-md"
        >
          <span>View on Xbox Store ↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- PC -->
      <div class="hud-card rounded-2xl p-6 border border-abyss-border space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-mono">
            PC (Epic Games Store)
          </span>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-abyss-card border border-abyss-border text-slate-300">Available</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          The definitive visual showcase powered by Unreal Engine 5. Supports unlocked framerates, ultra-wide 21:9 and 32:9 monitors, NVIDIA DLSS 3.5 Frame Generation, AMD FSR 3, and Intel XeSS.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-abyss-void/80 p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-abyss-border space-y-1 text-xs font-mono text-slate-300">
          <div><strong>Storefront:</strong> Epic Games Store (Steam release follows exclusivity)</div>
          <div><strong>Controller Support:</strong> DualSense, Xbox Wireless, Mouse &amp; Keyboard</div>
          <div><strong>Handheld:</strong> Fully verified on Steam Deck (via Heroic Launcher)</div>
        </div>
        <a
          href="https://store.epicgames.com/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="w-full py-2.5 px-4 rounded-xl bg-white hover:bg-slate-200 text-black font-semibold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-center block transition-colors shadow-md"
        >
          <span>Get on Epic Games Store ↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Nintendo Switch 2 -->
      <div class="hud-card rounded-2xl p-6 border border-abyss-border space-y-4" id="switch-2">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-mono">
            Nintendo Switch 2
          </span>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-abyss-card border border-abyss-border text-slate-300">Planned</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Industry reports indicate that Section 9 Interactive received next-generation Nintendo development kits. Given the Metroidvania structure and handheld appeal, an official announcement is expected alongside future console releases.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-abyss-void/80 p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-abyss-border space-y-1 text-xs font-mono text-slate-300">
          <div><strong>Status:</strong> Unannounced / In Active Development</div>
          <div><strong>Target Performance:</strong> 1080p Handheld (DLSS Reconstructed) / 60 FPS</div>
          <div><strong>Storefront:</strong> Nintendo eShop</div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- Tech Visual Banner -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-abyss-border">
      <img
        src="/images/platforms-tech.jpg"
        alt="End of Abyss System Specs and Tech Architecture"
        class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <FAQSection />

  </div>
</Layout>
